# =============================================================================
# Typeset frontend env
# =============================================================================
#
# The Anthropic API key lives in the OS keychain via the in-app Settings
# panel and is NOT pulled from this file.
#
# The two values below configure the public template-registry backend
# (Supabase). Without them, Typeset still works fully — the app just
# falls back to local-only template storage. With them, Typeset will
# auto-match dropped PDFs against the public registry and let users
# publish their own field maps.
#
# Get these from your Supabase project's `Settings → API` page:
#   - URL  → "Project URL"
#   - ANON → "anon public" key (NOT the service-role key)
#
# Both are safe to ship in a built binary: the anon key only grants the
# permissions defined by RLS in supabase/migrations/.
# =============================================================================

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
